<header class="hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">Dual-Engine AI Grid Framework</div>
  <h1>Predict the failure.<br>Isolate the fault.<br><span class="accent">Heal the grid — in milliseconds.</span></h1>
  <p>An interactive prototype of the AI-Powered Grid framework: Weibull-based equipment aging and Logistic Regression fused into a proactive risk engine, paired with a Breadth-First Search reconfiguration engine running on the real IEEE 33-bus topology. Below, the city is the grid — every building is a bus node.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a href="#demo" class="btn primary">Run the simulation ↓</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/Wann-xmh/AutoGrid/blob/main/Autogrid" target="_blank" class="btn">View source on GitHub ↗</a>
  </div>
  <div class="ticker">
    <div class="stat"><div class="num mono">85.33%</div><div class="lbl">Outage prediction accuracy</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num mono">33</div><div class="lbl">Bus IEEE test feeder</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num mono">&lt;1ms</div><div class="lbl">Reconfiguration response</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num mono">2025</div><div class="lbl">Cuba blackout, validated</div></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="demo">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="eyebrow">01 — Interactive Prototype</div>
    <h2>Break it yourself. Watch it heal.</h2>
    <p>This city block is a 1:1 render of the paper's IEEE 33-bus feeder (Table II), augmented with DER nodes. Click any building to mark its equipment as faulted — pick one bus or several at once — then activate self-healing and get a bus-by-bus solution report, checked against IEEE voltage and thermal-current limits.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo-shell">
    <div class="demo-top">
      <div class="canvas-wrap">
        <canvas id="cityCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="legend">
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#ffffff"></span>Main supply (bus 1)</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#5b6472"></span>Normal bus</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#e4483b"></span>Selected / faulted bus</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#333844"></span>Blacked-out (unreachable)</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#34d399"></span>Restored via tie-line</div>
          <div class="row"><span class="sw" style="background:#f5a623"></span>Islanded on local DER</div>
        </div>
        <div class="canvas-hint">click a building to mark a fault · drag to orbit · scroll to zoom</div>
        <div class="selected-chips" id="selectedChips"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="side-panel">
        <div class="block">
          <h4>Fault Selection</h4>
          <div id="selectionSummary" class="mono" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.7;">No buses selected. Click buildings in the city to mark broken equipment.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <h4>Line &amp; Voltage Compliance</h4>
          <div class="gauge-row"><span>Buses within ±5% voltage band</span><span class="val mono" id="voltCompliance">33/33</span></div>
          <div class="gauge-track"><div class="gauge-fill" id="voltFill" style="width:100%;background:var(--restore)"></div></div>
          <div class="gauge-row"><span>Branches within thermal rating</span><span class="val mono" id="currCompliance">—/—</span></div>
          <div class="gauge-track"><div class="gauge-fill" id="currFill" style="width:100%;background:var(--restore)"></div></div>
          <div class="eq-line" style="margin-top:8px;">Limits: 0.95 ≤ V ≤ 1.05 pu · |I_ij| ≤ I_ij,max (Eq. 5)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <h4>SCADA Event Log</h4>
          <div class="console" id="console">
            <div class="l">&gt; system idle. all 33 buses nominal.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-controls">
      <button class="ctrl-btn step2" id="btnCuba"><span class="step">PRESET</span>Load Cuba-Style Scenario (bus 15 &amp; 26)</button>
      <button class="ctrl-btn step3" id="btnHeal" disabled><span class="step">SELF-HEALING</span>Activate Self-Healing (BFS + FLISR)</button>
      <button class="ctrl-btn reset" id="btnClear">Clear Faults</button>
      <button class="ctrl-btn reset" id="btnReset">Reset Grid</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="modal-backdrop" id="modalBackdrop">
  <div class="modal">
    <div class="modal-head">
      <h3>Self-Healing Report</h3>
      <button class="modal-close" id="modalClose">Close ✕</button>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-body" id="modalBody"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<section id="methodology">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="eyebrow">02 — Methodology</div>
    <h2>Three mathematical layers, one pipeline</h2>
    <p>Each layer is computationally lightweight by design — logistic regression, closed-form Weibull CDFs, and standard graph search — so the framework runs on existing SCADA/DMS hardware with no new capital investment.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="idx">Layer 01</div>
      <h3>Degradation &amp; Risk Modeling</h3>
      <p>Transformer aging is modeled with the Weibull CDF (β &gt; 1, wear-out phase), fitted from IEEE historical failure data. Ambient temperature, grid load, and Weibull risk feed a logistic classifier for outage probability.</p>
      <div class="eq">Wrisk(t) = 1 − e^-(t/η)^β<br>ρ(outage) = 1 / (1 + e^-Z)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="idx">Layer 02</div>
      <h3>Graph Reconfiguration</h3>
      <p>On fault detection, a BFS traversal over the bus adjacency matrix instantly isolates the compromised branch. A constrained optimizer selects tie-switches that maximize restored critical load per switching operation.</p>
      <div class="eq">f_max = Σ ωᵢPᵢ − λN_sw<br>|I_ij| ≤ I_ij,max</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="idx">Layer 03</div>
      <h3>Root Cause Diagnosis</h3>
      <p>The linear score Z is disaggregated into thermal, load, and aging contributions, normalized, and ranked — producing an interpretable, single-cause diagnostic alert operators can act on immediately.</p>
      <div class="eq">Cᵢ = β·factorᵢ<br>RootCause = argmax(C_temp, C_load, C_age)</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="case-study">
  <div class="section-head">
    <div class="eyebrow">03 — Validation</div>
    <h2>The 2025 Cuba National Grid failure</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="case-grid">
    <div>
      <p>A single-point failure at Diezmero Substation cascaded into a nationwide blackout — the defining case study for why prediction, isolation, and restoration can no longer be solved as three separate problems.</p>
      <p>Without proactive monitoring, aging equipment and insufficient maintenance at Diezmero went undetected until the transformer or switchgear failed outright. The interconnected system had no automated way to isolate the compromised section, so the fault propagated unchecked across the island.</p>
      <p>The framework demoed above addresses each failure point directly: Weibull + logistic scoring would have flagged Diezmero as high-risk ahead of time; BFS-driven FLISR would have isolated the fault and rerouted critical loads through DERs before cascade — the same sequence you just triggered on the city grid.</p>
